{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"marine-herby-wolf","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Not the same bug as [rebar:895c-3eb2-043a-4de1] — do not fold them together\n\nWhile proving 895c's root cause (Bedrock rejecting an over-complex structured-output grammar), a\n**second, distinct** LLM failure mode surfaced in the same logs and must not be attributed to it.\n\n### The two are separable on three independent axes\n\n| | 895c (schema complexity) | THIS bug (overlap-judge) |\n|---|---|---|\n| step | `plan-review-prerequisite-verifier` | `overlap-judge` |\n| duration | 180.6-185.9s (tight, 27 samples) | **312-381s** (different band) |\n| `requests` recorded | **0** — no model request ever completed (pre-response 400) | **3** — real requests completed |\n\nA pre-response 400 and a failure after three completed requests are different mechanisms. The\nduration bands do not overlap.\n\n### What is known\n\n* Recorded via the usage instrumentation landed by [rebar:aec1-76e7-bb95-4c86]: 5 occurrences,\n  312-381s, `requests=3`. Overall failure rate across that sample was 64 ok / 9 failed = 12.3%.\n* Separately observed in `/tmp/03ef-review6.out`: `llm call [overlap-judge] ... model=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 FAILED in 0.4s: status_code: 401 ... 'API key is invalid.'` — a DIFFERENT overlap-judge failure again (direct-Anthropic auth), tracked separately.\n* 895c's original report also noted `UnexpectedModelBehavior: Exceeded maximum output retries (2)`\n  from the overlap judge — consistent with an output/validation failure rather than a request\n  rejection.\n\n### Why it matters\n\n`overlap-judge` deduplicates findings across reviewers. When it fails the review still proceeds,\nso this degrades silently — the failure is not visible in the verdict.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the mechanism behind the 312-381s / `requests=3` overlap-judge failures is established BY\n      MEASUREMENT (capture the actual exception and provider body — the existing evidence records\n      duration and request count but not the error body)\n- [ ] it is confirmed whether this is retry exhaustion, an output-validation failure, or a\n      provider-side timeout — the three imply different fixes\n- [ ] the effect of an overlap-judge failure on the resulting verdict is stated explicitly: what\n      silently changes when dedup does not run\n- [ ] a regression test drives the identified failure path\n\n## Testing\n\n    python -m rebar.llm.usage_log summarize .rebar/usage.jsonl   # the recorded evidence\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -q","id":"2391-a941-69ff-4645","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"overlap-judge LLM calls fail at 312-381s with requests=3 — a SECOND failure mode, distinct from the schema-complexity 400"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785958384886245001,"uuid":"f676377a-8868-4bae-9c84-fefdc2a5c20a"}